+# FAA Operations Center visit drafts name different possible record recipients
+
+Reviewed November 9, 2026 Eastern. B129 / PD01 / PD07. Three Commission archive members supply two working copies of a visit memorandum, handwritten visit notes and a separately filed roster. The working copies and the archived NARA memorandum preserve different dates and wording about where FAA information went. That wording supplies leads to agency transfer and receipt records.
+
+## Dates and source lineage
+
+| Record | Visible observation |
+| --- | --- |
+| Team 8 Box 18 item 079, physical pp. 1–5 | P. 1 lines 3–8 read **FAA OPS CENTER VISIT 2/6/2003** in the subject and **Date of visit: 2/4/2003** in a separate field. The copy identifies John Raidt as preparer, refers to an attached participant roster and says the meeting began at approximately 1 p.m. |
+| Same item, physical pp. 6–10 | The marked-up working copy's p. 6 lines 3–8 give **Date of visit: 6/4/2003** and the roster reference. The scan shows editing marks in the body. |
+| Archived NARA item 00244, physical p. 1 lines 8–21 | The opening visit memorandum gives **6/4/2003** and identifies Raidt and Team 7. The two later follow-up copies at pp. 6 and 8 have a distinct February year-marking issue, preserved in the earlier review. |
+| Team 8 Box 4 item 777, physical pp. 1 and 8, and Box 18 item 175, p. 1 | The handwritten notes' p. 1 header shows **6/4/03** beside crossed-out writing. Both roster faces show **6/4/03** and the same distinctive crossed-out line and entry arrangement. Item 175 masks part of the roster. Item 777 includes a roster face as p. 8. |
+
+The versions share closely matching passages on the start time, a chronology under preparation and the telephone nets. The roster comparison is visual. The visible layout supports a shared page source, with no proof that either exact scan was the cited attachment or that every listed person attended. Item 079 also contains three pages headed **Page 1 of 27** through **Page 3 of 27** from separate forwarded material at pp. 11–13. Those pages sit outside the two working-copy spans. Keep the two February 2003 fields, June 2003 fields, crossed-out notes and later follow-up dates separate. A dated meeting or document-control record could establish version order and confirm which date fields refer to the same visit.
+
+[Public ZIP containing exact items 079, 175 and 777](https://archive.org/download/911datasets/NARA_9-11_Commission_Records_Released_Jan_14_2009.zip) · [Official archived memorandum, NAID 2609836](https://nara-media-001.s3.amazonaws.com/arcmedia/9-11/MFR/t-0148-911MFR-00244.pdf) · [Prior reading of the February follow-up copies](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/24561a8a9f28e5a33ebe3ea7ddeb8ea34af794e2/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-operations-center-mfr-route-2026-11-05/README.md)
+
+## Custody claims and contrary evidence
+
+| Locator | Observation | What it can support |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Item 079, p. 2 lines 32–38 | The working copy says FAA reported that most information about what happened that day was transferred **“to TSA.”** | A reported transfer to investigate. The sentence gives no inventory or accession. |
+| Item 079, p. 7 lines 35–41 | The other copy visibly adds underlined text to give **“to TSA, to NTSB or to the FBI.”** Its extracted text at line 38 has **“to TSA. to NTSB or to the FBI.”** | Preserve the two readings and the broader agency list. The rendering shows an editorial mark. The sentence still supplies no agency-by-item allocation or transfer date. |
+| Archived item 00244, p. 2 lines 44–50 | The archived wording visibly retains **“to TSA, to NTSB or to the FBI.”** All three typed passages report FAA's **“NO recording of the Phone Bridge”** beside Ken Mead's account of hearing that there was a recording and that it went to DoJ. | The agency list and bridge accounts were recorded together. The reported transfer of most information and the possible transfer of one recording are separate claims. Mead's account is attributed to an earlier meeting and gives no item number, receiving acknowledgment or recorder identity. |
+| Handwritten item 777, p. 1 upper block and p. 2 lower half | P. 1 refers to work on a master chronology. P. 2 sketches the primary and secondary nets, refers to an operations-center log with participants and reads **“no tape (our lines didn't record on 9/11)”** in the telephone-net area. | The phrase “our lines” preserves the note's scope. The notes point to a possible participant log. They supply neither a recorder configuration nor a transfer or receipt. |
+
+The reported FAA chronology for the Secretary's chief of staff appears in both working copies and the archived memorandum. The contemporaneous memo and notes give a date and a subject to use in the search. Their relationship to the final chronology, any corrected QFR, or the wording later reported by the Inspector General remains open. The repeated statements across memo copies are related records. The same text appearing twice supplies no independent verification of transfer or recording. [Archived visit account, PDF pp. 1–2](https://nara-media-001.s3.amazonaws.com/arcmedia/9-11/MFR/t-0148-911MFR-00244.pdf#page=1) · [OIG report, printed p. 12](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/cc2006085.pdf#page=13)
+
+## Verification and open inputs
+
+Three exact ZIP members were verified against the central-directory path, CRC and byte length and retained with hashes. The comparison screened all 22 newly retrieved pages for extractable text. Visual checks covered the two working-copy headers and transfer paragraphs, the archived transfer paragraph, the scoped handwritten passages and the two roster layouts. Locators give physical pages and PyMuPDF extraction lines where applicable. The reading was scoped to provenance, the chronology and transfer accounts. Source scans and contact fields are excluded from this derivative. [Source pins](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+- [ ] **PD07.** Seek the dated master chronology, its working versions, a copy routed to the chief of staff and a delivery or accession record. Separately seek the roster and dated meeting control tying the visit fields to the actual event.
+- [ ] **PD01 / PD07.** Seek the original operations-center participant log, agency-by-agency transfer inventories and receipt records, and bridge channel and recorder documentation. If an original or duplicate recording surfaces, compare it to the primary and secondary nets and the separate promised filtered ATC audio before making a source match.
+- [ ] **PD01–PD04.** Keep the actual corrected May 2003 answer, receiving acknowledgment, signed consideration or action/no-action decision and recommendation-specific outcomes as distinct open inputs.
